          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(3\\cos\\theta+4\\sin\\theta)^2-(4\\cos\\theta-3\\sin\\theta)^2&=\\begin{aligned}&9\\cos^2\\theta+24\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta+16\\sin^2\\theta\\\\&-16\\cos^2\\theta+24\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta-9\\sin^2\\theta\\end{aligned}\\\\(3\\cos\\theta+4\\sin\\theta)^2-(4\\cos\\theta-3\\sin\\theta)^2&=7\\sin^2\\theta+48\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta-7\\cos^2\\theta\\end{align*}$$\nAt $\\theta=0^\\circ$, the expression equals $-7$. At $\\theta=90^\\circ$, it equals $7$. These different values show that the expression depends on $\\theta$.",
